Design system
=============

Colour
------

src/theme/tokens.js is the only place a colour is defined. No screen contains
a literal hex value.

	Field        bg0 #0C1530  bg1 #13214D  bg2 #19294F  appBg #0C1530
	Surfaces     card, card2        translucent white over the navy
	             cardLine, cardLine2 hairline borders
	Ink          text #EEF3FA  text2 #A8BBD4  text3 #6E84A4
	Blue         blue #2F7BC4  blue2 #4A93D8  blueSoft  blueLine
	Gold         gold #FFD157  goldDim #E0A838  goldSoft  goldLine
	             goldInk #2A1E04 for text sitting on gold
	Podium       medalGold, medalSilver #C6CDD8, medalBronze #C8884E,
	             each with a Dim companion
	Status       green #4FB587, coral #E07A5F, plum #A98BC9

Surfaces are translucent white over the navy field rather than solid panels.
That is what gives the app its depth, and it is why a solid background colour
on a card looks immediately wrong.

Gold is the single functional accent: the primary action, the raised tab
button, the current position, first place, the back affordance. Spending it on
decoration costs it its meaning.


Type
----

src/theme/typography.js.

	Display   Space Grotesk   400, 500, 600, 700
	Body      Inter           400, 500, 600

React Native has no weight axis, so each weight is a separate registered
family. The names in typography.js must match the useFonts keys in App.js
exactly; a mismatch fails silently to the system font.

The type helper exposes ready-made styles with letter spacing already
converted from em to the absolute values React Native expects.


Iconography and art
-------------------

No icon library. Everything is drawn.

	components/Glyphs.js       general SVG glyph registry
	components/icons.js        navigation and UI icons
	components/SportIcons.js   activity and sport icons
	components/KnightAvatar.js the SVG avatar fallback

Real art lives in assets/:

	assets/avatars/faculty1..faculty9/1..5.png    avatar per faculty per tier
	assets/facultyBadges/1..9.png                 faculty crests
	assets/brand/uwindsor-logo.png
	assets/animations/*.json                      Lottie

Faculty keys faculty1 through faculty9 map index for index onto both folders.
The backend assigns the key from the student's faculty; the client never
guesses it.

	data/avatarSources.js         build-time require map for avatar art
	data/facultyBadgeSources.js   build-time require map for crests
	data/facultyTheme.js          the nine themes, tier names, tierForLevel,
	                              getAvatarSource, themeForFaculty

Metro resolves require() paths at bundle time, so every path in those two maps
must point at a file that exists. A dynamic path will not work.


Shared components
-----------------

	ui.js                   primitives shared across screens
	GlassTitle.js           the frosted page title
	GoldBackHeader.js       the gold text-only back affordance
	TabBar.js               the custom tab bar with the raised centre button
	BottomSheetModal.js     the sheet primitive
	Overlays.js             the sheet and modal host
	FacultyAvatar.js        the right avatar for a faculty and level
	FacultyBadge.js         the crest inside its glass box
	DynamicLeaderboardBoard.js  podium plus rows, grouped or per user
	Badge.js, BadgeSheet.js, BadgeAwardModal.js, LevelUpModal.js
	stats/StatBarChart.js, StatTiles.js, StatHeroMetric.js,
	stats/RangeSelector.js, stats/HomeStatsWidget.js

PressScale, used for tap feedback, applies its style to an inner animated view
and takes a separate wrapStyle for the outer pressable. If a row of pressables
will not spread evenly, the flex belongs on wrapStyle. This has been diagnosed
more than once.


Layout rules
------------

* Page titles are left aligned with a gold edge bar. Centred titles with
  horizontal padding were the source of a recurring complaint about a gap
  before the title, and the pattern has been removed from every sheet and
  screen. Do not reintroduce it.
* A screen's horizontal padding belongs to one element. Putting a padded
  header inside an already padded scroll view doubles the inset; every screen
  puts its header outside the scroll view in a root view for this reason.
* Safe area insets are applied with a clamp, not raw, so the header does not
  drift on devices with a large top inset.
* Locked or unearned states are shown, not hidden. A badge a student has not
  earned and a tier they have not reached both render, dimmed.


Copy
----

* No emoji. Flag characters on the leaderboard are data, not decoration.
* No em dashes.
* Sentence case for labels. Uppercase is reserved for eyebrow labels.
* Numbers are the point of this app. Never truncate one to fit a layout.